  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14253719/assets/3af9e0f9483bf968ebf0db637e74c0536f19d4da6f15895d03ab04f39d1d98b0.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $a+b?$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we have to find $a+b.$ According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $a+b$ goes from the tail of $a$ to the head of $b:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14253719/assets/f95b72a0b508e0cdacef7de386888f3b473aeba01574ce5fb345b9fec74bb900.png)\n\nIn $△AHB$, we have $∠AHB={90}^{∘}$, $AH=2$ and $BH=2.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+b| & =AB \\\\  & =\\sqrt{A{H}^{2}+B{H}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $a+b$ is $2\\sqrt{2}.$ Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{1}{|a+b|}\\cdot (a+b) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}(a+b).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
